 nd Latin influences\, Spencer explores the cultural connections between Me
 xico and the U.S.---and the unexpected ways music can bring us together. T
 his special evening will feature brand-new songs and arrangements from La 
 Frontera alongside favorites from Spencer's celebrated catalog\, plus a ve
 ry special guest musician from Mexico. With his signature mix of sophistic
 ated musicianship\, storytelling and humor\, Spencer invites audiences to 
 be among the first to experience where his music is headed next. A new cha
 pter. A special homecoming. A first listen. Don't miss Spencer Day at Fein
 stein's at the Nikko. From the Artist \, "rdquo" -> I've spent the last fe
 w years falling ever deeper in love with Mexico---not just with the music\
 , but with the people\, the culture and the way so many of our traditions 
 coexist\," says Day. \, "rdquo" -> La Frontera grew out of that experience
 . It's about more than just the border---it's about what happens when cult
 ures meet\, influence one another and create something new. It's a meditat
 ion on the many things that connect us and divide us. I'm incredibly excit
 ed to share it for the first time with the city that gave me my start. San
  Francisco has always 
LOCATION:222 Mason Street\, San Francisco\, CA
